### Desk Companion Backend API smoke tests
### Use with VS Code REST Client or IntelliJ HTTP Client

### Environment variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
### IMPORTANT: must be a valid UUID format, otherwise GET/PUT profile returns HTTP 400.
@userId = 73f8a65c-fd87-41f1-ac68-3a00b83e1211


### 1) Register new account
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "displayName": "桌面小夥伴"
}


### 2) Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_user@example.com",
  "password": "Password456!"
}

### 2) Login failure
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_uer@example.com",
  "password": "Password456!"
}


### 3) Validation failure test (invalid email + short password + blank displayName)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "123",
  "displayName": ""
}


### 4) Get profile by userId
### Option A: manually set @userId above with a valid UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json


### 4-2) Get profile from register response (VS Code REST Client)
### Uses id from step 1 response body: { "id": "..." }
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{register.response.body.$.id}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json


### 4-3) Get profile from login response (VS Code REST Client)
### Uses userId from step 2 response body: { "userId": "..." }
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{login.response.body.$.userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json


### 5) Update profile by userId
### Option A: manually set @userId above with a valid UUID
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "桌面小夥伴-更新",
  "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/avatar.png"
}


### 5-2) Update profile from login response (VS Code REST Client)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{login.response.body.$.userId}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "桌面小夥伴-更新-2",
  "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/avatar-2.png"
}

### 6) Forgot password
### resetToken only returns when app.auth.return-reset-token-for-testing=true
# @name forgotPassword
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_user@example.com"
}




### 7-1) Validate reset token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/validate-reset-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_user@example.com",
  "token": "{{forgotPassword.response.body.$.resetToken}}"
}

### 7) Reset password
### Replace reset token with value from step 6 response body.resetToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_user@example.com",
  "token": "{{forgotPassword.response.body.$.resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "Password456!"
}


### 8) Soft delete account
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{login.response.body.$.userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Password456!"
}

### 9) account recovery
# @name recoveryAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/account-recovery
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_user@example.com",
  "password": "Password456!"
}

### 10) account-recovery-confirm
# @name recoveryConfirm
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/account-recovery/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test_user@example.com",
  "token": "{{recoveryAccount.response.body.$.recoveryToken}}"
}
